+(duration-opts)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit: `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m`
+(minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear at most once and in that order, with no spaces in between. Units are
+case-insensitive, so `2d`, `1h30m`, `45S`, `1d2h3m4s`, and `90m` are all valid. A value that is already a
+{class}`~datetime.timedelta` is returned unchanged.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
